    "result_text": "All tests pass with a clean build. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: household-capped membership level\n\n**Spec:** A new owner's `membershipLevel` cannot exceed one above the current maximum `membershipLevel` among their household members; the capped level is returned. With no existing household member, no cap applies.\n\n### What I found\n`membershipLevel` is a read-time derived field (`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`) computed from `membershipPoints`. The cap depends on household members' levels at creation time, so \u2014 like the existing `namesakeCount`/`householdSize` snapshots \u2014 it must be captured at creation and persisted.\n\nThe new acceptance test also creates **two owners in the same household** (same last name + postcode) with *different* telephones and expects both to succeed. The old `rejectDuplicateIdentity` rejected any second owner sharing a `householdId` with a 409, contradicting the documented identity-key semantics (openapi: *\"Two owners are treated as duplicates only when their whole identity keys match\"*).\n\n### Edits\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `membershipLevelCap` field (nullable) with accessors.\n2. **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `membership_level_cap` column so the snapshot survives a reload (tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, and every read re-derives the level).\n3. **`OwnerMapper.membershipLevel`** \u2014 after deriving the 1\u20134 level, caps it: `min(level, cap)` when a cap is present; unchanged otherwise. Stays within the openapi `[1,4]` bounds.\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`**:\n   - `rejectDuplicateIdentity` now compares the full identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`, reusing `OwnerMapper.identityKey`) instead of `householdId` alone \u2014 so same-household owners differing in telephone/email are admitted as additional members, matching the documented spec.\n   - Added `membershipLevelCap(householdId)` (one above the highest effective level among existing non-deleted household members, or `null` when none) and snapshot it onto the owner at creation.\n\n### Verification\n- `coreCapsLevelByHousehold`: both owners created (levels 1 and 2), `lb \u2264 la + 1` holds.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test, 0 failures.",
